  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="8b2410d3-bb2b-4626-b7a5-1bd9f96a758a"><problem><para>
      <para>A rocket is launched in the air and its height, in feet, is modeled by the function \(h\).</para>
      <para>Here is a graph representing \(h\).</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="A curve on a graph, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis, time, seconds, scale 0 to 8, by 1’s. Vertical axis, height, feet, scale 0 to 200, by 20’s. A curve passes through the points 0 comma 5, 3 comma 161, and 5 comma 105."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/d4c68792388451be9621c700e4f27732ae382c2c"/></media></figure></para>
      <para><emphasis>Select three</emphasis> true statements about the situation.</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>["The rocket is launched from a height less than 20 feet above the ground.", "The rocket reaches its maximum height after about 3 seconds.", "The maximum height of the rocket is about 160 feet." ]</para><para>
      <para>The correct answers are: The rocket is launched from a height less than 20 feet above the ground. The rocket
        reaches its maximum height after about 3 seconds. The maximum height of the rocket is about 160 feet. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
